       'Write the mark scheme in the matching style: point-based schemes for short items (one mark per creditworthy point, with the acceptable alternatives), levelled schemes for extended items (level descriptors with indicative content), and the rules for working, units and partially correct answers.',
       'Write model answers: a full-mark answer and a mid-band answer for every extended item, annotated to show where the marks are gained and lost, so markers and students can see the standard.',
       'Check the paper: timing at a realistic words-per-mark rate for the age, reading load, accessibility (no item depends on a diagram without a described alternative), and that no question leaks the answer to another.',
